---
import LandingLayout from '../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../../components/HeroSection.astro';
import CenteredTextBlock from '../../components/CenteredTextBlock.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import FaqItem from '../../components/FaqItem.astro';
import TestimonialSlideshow from '../../components/TestimonialSlideshow.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
import FeatureGrid from '../../components/FeatureGrid.astro';
import FeatureCard from '../../components/FeatureCard.astro';
import TimelineSection from '../../components/TimelineSection.astro';
import TimelineItem from '../../components/TimelineItem.astro';
import ChecklistSection from '../../components/ChecklistSection.astro';
import PricingCallout from '../../components/PricingCallout.astro';
import ImageTextSplit from '../../components/ImageTextSplit.astro';
import HighlightPanel from '../../components/HighlightPanel.astro';
import VideoSection from '../../components/VideoSection.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../../components/CtaBanner.astro';

const reviewIds = ['c83dba55', 'fcb52150', '94fe245a'];

const navLinks = [
  { label: 'Why DJ Misha', href: '#features' },
  { label: 'Timeline', href: '#timeline' },
  { label: 'Package', href: '#package' },
  { label: 'Pricing', href: '#pricing' },
  { label: 'FAQ', href: '#faq' },
];
---

<LandingLayout
  title="Design Guide - DJ Misha"
  description="Design guide page demonstrating reusable page components"
  noindex={true}
>
  <HeroSection
    backgroundImage="/images/banner.jpg"
    alt="Wedding DJ in San Diego"
    scrollTarget="#intro"
  >
    <p slot="headline">The Perfect Soundtrack for Your Special Day</p>
    <h1 slot="title">Wedding DJ in San Diego</h1>
  </HeroSection>

  <CenteredTextBlock id="intro" align="left">
    <h2>The Perfect Soundtrack for Your Special Day</h2>
    <p>
      Think about the most fun wedding you've attended. What do you remember?
      There's a good chance your time on the dance floor stands out. The music
      was pumping; the atmosphere was electric; and every song seemed to capture
      the essence of the couple's love story. That's the kind of unforgettable
      experience <a href="/about/" rel="nofollow" title="">DJ Misha</a> strives to
      create.
    </p>
    <p>
      The music is one of the most important parts of the reception, and with DJ
      Misha, it's not just about playing track after track — it's about creating
      a seamless blend of music that enhances the overall atmosphere of the
      night. He works closely with every couple to <a
        href="/blog/your-wedding-your-music-how-i-spin-a-dj-set-tailored-to-your-vision/"
        title="Your Wedding, Your Music: How I Spin a DJ Set Tailored to Your Vision"
        >design the perfect live DJ set</a
      >, making their wedding a dance party that creates lasting memories for
      years to come.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >Your wedding is about you. Let's make the music match your vision.</strong
      >
    </p>
  </CenteredTextBlock>

  <SectionNav links={navLinks} />

  <FeatureGrid
    id="features"
    eyebrow="Why DJ Misha"
    heading="Why Choose DJ Misha for Your Wedding"
    alt={true}
  >
    <FeatureCard title="Crafts a Personalized Music Experience" icon="star">
      <p>
        By tailoring a new set list for every event, DJ Misha transforms each
        wedding into a one-of-a-kind music experience that reflects your unique
        tastes and preferences. He collaborates with you to plan the perfect
        playlist to tell your story, ensuring that the music remains perfectly
        suited to the moment by monitoring the energy of the room and adjusting
        his set to keep the atmosphere lively and upbeat.
      </p>
    </FeatureCard>
    <FeatureCard
      title="Blends Technical Skill & Artistic Talent"
      icon="lightbulb"
    >
      <p>
        Throughout DJ Misha's career, he has focused on collecting and curating
        music that drives dance floor energy and taps into the audience's
        emotions. His passion for the technical and aesthetic art of DJing is
        what makes him stand out above the rest. He believes music should be a
        cohesive experience. By bringing a unique sound to every wedding, DJ
        Misha creates a feeling that lasts long after the music stops.
      </p>
    </FeatureCard>
    <FeatureCard title="Creates a Memorable Celebration" icon="check">
      <p>
        Whether you're local to San Diego or having a destination wedding, DJ
        Misha is focused on entertaining you and your guests during the most
        special day of your life, which is why he is dedicated to creating
        something special just for you. He curates playlists that flow
        seamlessly, engage your guests, and capture the essence of your
        celebration. At the end of the day, he wants to bring your vision to
        life, so you can dance the night away with friends and family.
      </p>
    </FeatureCard>
  </FeatureGrid>

  <TimelineSection
    id="timeline"
    eyebrow="The night"
    heading="The Timeline of Your Wedding Day Music"
  >
    <TimelineItem title="Ceremony">
      <p>
        The ceremony is magical. No matter how many times you witness one,
        you're bound to get the chills and feel emotional. For a perfect
        execution, here's what to consider.
      </p>
      <ul class="wp-block-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Before the Ceremony: </strong>Play soft music about 30 minutes
          before the start, as the guests are arriving and taking their seats.
          Once the ceremony is ready to begin, an announcement will likely be
          made for guests to take their seats.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Wedding Procession: </strong>The arrival of the groom, family,
          ring bearer, and flower girls can each all walk down the aisle to one
          song. A different song should be played for the arrival of the bride,
          highlighting their unique entrance.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>During the Ceremony:</strong> You'll want to have a quality microphone
          for the officiant. It's a good idea to practice with the officiant for the
          moments when they'll need to turn the mic to the couple to give their vows.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>After the Ceremony:</strong> Choose a powerful and exciting song
          for the couple to walk off together after the ceremony.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To put all of this together, you'll need a good sound technician to
        control the volume, make the transitions at the right moments, and
        prevent any issues like microphone feedback or volume being too low for
        guests to hear.
      </p>
    </TimelineItem>

    <TimelineItem title="Cocktail Hour">
      <p>
        Following the ceremony, most weddings move to the cocktail hour, where
        guests can grab a drink, some appetizers, and socialize before they move
        into the dinner venue. For the bride, groom and family, this is often
        the time for photos.
      </p>
      <ul class="wp-block-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Type of Music:</strong> The music during the cocktail hour is passive
          and sets the mood for the night. The volume should be medium since it's
          not the main focus. You could hire an instrumental musician, or you could
          make a playlist for our DJ to play.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>End of the Cocktail Hour: </strong>Towards the end of the
          hour, an announcement can be made to ask people to take their seats at
          dinner.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </TimelineItem>

    <TimelineItem title="Dinner & Toasts">
      <p>
        During dinner the music is once again in the background with the volume
        at a low to medium level. Keep in mind the music will often be
        interrupted by other activities.
      </p>
      <ul class="wp-block-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Introducing the Wedding Party: </strong>Before dinner, the
          wedding party is typically introduced. Pick one song for their
          entrance, and make sure all names are clearly spelled out on your
          wedding timeline so that they are easy to read and pronounce.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Toasts: </strong>Giving toasts<strong> </strong>requires
          special attention. They almost always go longer than expected, so you
          should plan for an additional 30 minutes. Since most people aren't
          public speakers, help prepare them by sending a few tips and maybe a
          short YouTube video with best practices. This can make a big
          difference!
        </li>
      </ul>
    </TimelineItem>

    <TimelineItem title="Dancing">
      <p>
        During the dancing portion of the evening, the music moves into the
        forefront. The volume goes up; there are fewer interruptions, if any;
        and people are on the dance floor having a good time.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Dancing is the time for your DJ to shine</strong>, and if you've
        chosen the right one, they'll bring their A game on your special
        evening. Hopefully you're giving them the autonomy to do their best work
        – from there the only thing left to do is to have fun, enjoy yourself,
        and dance the night away.
      </p>
    </TimelineItem>
  </TimelineSection>

  <ImageTextSplit
    image="/images/Best-San-Diego-DJ-djmisha.com-12-300x200.jpg"
    alt="DJ Misha performing"
    caption="DJ Misha performing for Pacific Magazine"
  >
    <h2>From Clubs to Corporate Events</h2>
    <p>
      Keeping the dance floor moving is the top priority — a renowned
      performance that has rocked stages from the W Hotel to corporate events
      and private parties coast to coast.
    </p>
  </ImageTextSplit>

  <HighlightPanel heading="What does a DJ do?" icon="lightbulb" alt={true}>
    <p>
      There are two responsibilities at the core of DJ'ing: curating excellent
      music that captivates a specific audience, and mixing it seamlessly to
      create a set that holds the crowd's energy all night.
    </p>
  </HighlightPanel>

  <ChecklistSection
    id="package"
    eyebrow="Included"
    heading="Wedding DJ Service Package"
  >
    <ul>
      <li>DJ to handle music and MC announcements</li>
      <li>Event planning session and timeline review</li>
      <li>Coordination between vendors and planners</li>
      <li>Full music consultation</li>
      <li>2 high-powered speakers and DJ booth</li>
      <li>Microphone for toasts and announcements</li>
    </ul>
  </ChecklistSection>

  <PricingCallout id="pricing" price="$2,500" caption="Average wedding rate">
    <p>
      <strong
        >On average you can expect to pay about $2500 for our wedding DJ
        services in San Diego.</strong
      > This popular package includes 4 hours of coverage for the reception, with
      a 2-speaker sound system and a microphone for toasts. Keep in mind rates can
      vary based on factors like the length of the event, number of people attending,
      customization options, equipment rental, travel expenses, and if live saxophone
      music is included. Couples should communicate their specific needs and budget
      to ensure a clear understanding of the services provided and any associated
      costs.
    </p>
  </PricingCallout>

  <VideoSection
    videoId="Mj10etssu9E"
    title="DJ Misha live performance"
    eyebrow="Watch"
    heading="See DJ Misha in Action"
    alt={true}
  />

  <FaqSection id="faq" eyebrow="FAQ" heading="Frequently Asked Questions">
    <FaqItem question="Can a Wedding DJ Take Song Requests?">
      <p>
        Absolutely, and the decision is entirely up to you. Your DJ is available
        to take requests if that is something you would like. Sometimes,
        requests can provide useful feedback from the audience and add a fun,
        interactive element to the party. However, our primary commitment is to
        you. The DJ will always prioritize your vision and the seamless flow of
        the musical journey we've planned together, ensuring any request fits
        the atmosphere and never disrupts the energy on the dance floor.
      </p>
    </FaqItem>
    <FaqItem question="What Questions Should I Ask My Wedding DJ?">
      <p>
        Before hiring a wedding DJ, you'll want to ask certain questions to make
        sure they meet your needs for your special day. Here are some helpful
        questions to consider: What is your experience with DJ-ing weddings? How
        many have you done? Do you have testimonials from past clients? Do you
        have backup equipment in case of technical issues? How do you handle
        song requests and do-not-play lists? Can you make announcements during
        the event? Do you offer additional services? What is your policy on
        overtime? Is there an additional charge? How far in advance should we
        book your services? What is your cancellation or rescheduling policy?
      </p>
    </FaqItem>
    <FaqItem question="How Many Hours Does a DJ Play at a Wedding?">
      <p>
        Our DJ services can be used throughout the entirety of your wedding day,
        from before the ceremony to the end of the reception. Our wedding
        package typically includes 4 hours of reception music. Custom packages
        can be created based on your individual needs.
      </p>
    </FaqItem>
    <FaqItem question="Does DJ Misha Perform at Destination Weddings?">
      <p>
        Yes! DJ Misha is available for national and international travel.
        Whether you're in San Diego or hosting a destination wedding in a unique
        location, he can bring the music to you. Reach out to us with details
        like your wedding location and date, because travel to any destination
        is possible. For destination weddings, DJ Misha will take care of all
        travel booking and equipment rentals that are required for a remote
        performance, ensuring there is no additional work for you. He will also
        handle all the coordination between vendors and event planners too,
        making your destination wedding planning an easy and efficient process.
      </p>
    </FaqItem>
  </FaqSection>

  <TestimonialSlideshow
    reviewIds={reviewIds}
    eyebrow="Kind words"
    heading="What Clients Say"
  />

  <CtaBanner href="/contact/" buttonLabel="Book Your Date">
    <h2>Let's rock your wedding party together</h2>
    <p>Send your date, location, and any details — you'll get a quick reply.</p>
  </CtaBanner>
</LandingLayout>
